course: dictionary
lesson: 222
title: Alive: living, lively and still going
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Alive usually means living, not dead. A fish, a dog or a child is alive. A stone was never alive, and a fallen leaf is no longer alive. «Hold a magnifying glass over an ant and the bent light makes the ant look huge.» The ant is alive, so it can move, breathe and feed.
explain: Alive can also mean full of energy or life. «Yet the biggest animal of all time is not a lost monster but alive today.» Here alive means the blue whale still exists now. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: the blue whale is living today, so the meaning fits.
explain: Look at the words around alive to choose the right meaning. «Most of the energy an animal eats is used for moving, growing, keeping warm and staying alive.» Staying alive means continuing to live. «Some friendships last a lifetime, kept alive by lots of small calls and visits» means the friendship keeps going because people keep it going.
fact: Alive means living, not dead.
fact: Alive can mean full of energy, activity or life, as in a town that «comes alive» at night.
fact: Alive can mean still existing or working, like a hope or a tradition.
fact: Living things move, grow, breathe, feed, sense and reproduce, so scientists sort things into alive, dead and never alive.
fact: Useful phrases with alive: «keep alive», «stay alive», «alive and well», and «alive with», which means full of.
exercise: «Most of the energy an animal eats is used for moving, growing, keeping warm and staying alive.» What does staying alive mean here? | *Continuing to live | Being full of noise and energy | Sitting very still | Turning into a plant
exercise: Which of these things is alive? | A stone on the beach | *A fish swimming in the sea | A dusty old book | A fallen leaf
exercise: Grandma says, «The old tradition is still alive in our village.» What does alive mean? | Living in a tree | Dead and buried | *Still existing and carried on | Loud, but only at night
test: «Some friendships last a lifetime, kept alive by lots of small calls and visits.» What does kept alive mean? | *Kept going, so it stays strong | Made into a film | Put in a glass box | Forgotten and left behind
test: Mia says the festival is «alive with music». What does alive with mean? | Empty of music | *Full of music and people | Hidden under music | Dead from too much music
exam: «The blue whale, up to about 30 metres long, is alive today.» Which meaning of alive fits best? | Hidden deep in the sea | Made of metal and glass | Dead and gone | *Living right now, not dead
